.UPDATE...
Issued at 920 AM PDT Thu Sep 24 2026

Thursday is the last day of warm conditions this week, maintaining
moderate HeatRisk across the interior East/South Bay valleys and Big
Sur coastline. A parade of high clouds ahead of a dry cold front
pushes through today with the actual frontal passage occurring
overnight. Early Friday morning, a mix of low and high clouds with
moderate to strong onshore winds, around 15 to 20 mph primarily at
the coast, will result in widespread cooler conditions Friday into
the weekend. No precipitation is expected with this system as it
cruises through the Bay Area and Central Coast.

