.AVIATION...
(18Z TAFS)
Issued at 1032 AM PDT Thu Sep 24 2026

VFR. The lack of a better defined marine layer has resulted in
VFR conditions regionwide this morning. Onshore winds are forecast
to increase through late morning and become locally gusty at
times this afternoon. Winds ease slightly late in the night before
a dry frontal boundary pushes southward across the region
overnight and into Friday morning. The greatest potential for MVFR
or sub-MVFR conditions will be early Friday morning around HAF,
OAK, and MRY. In wake of the frontal passage on Friday, expecting
an increase north-northwesterly winds.

Vicinity of SFO...VFR through the TAF period. Onshore winds
increase this afternoon and again in wake of the early morning dry
frontal passage. There is a 20-30 percent probability of MVFR
ceilings just before sunrise on Friday, yet the greatest potential
will be over OAK. Thus, have left out of the TAFs at this time.

SFO Bridge Approach...Similar to SFO.

Monterey Bay Terminals...VFR. Onshore winds increase this
afternoon and ease after sunset. The greatest probability of sub-
MVFR conditions will be at MRY just before sunrise. Once the dry
frontal boundary passes, any low clouds that do develop will mix
out by around 17Z.

